<header><p class="enc-kicker">Work / monument · monument</p><h1 class="enc-title">St. Olaf's Church, Tallinn</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">St. Olaf's Church is a Gothic church in the old town of Tallinn, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/estonia">Estonia</a>, first recorded in the 13th century. Rebuilt several times after fires and lightning strikes, its spire is thought to have made it one of the tallest buildings in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/europe">Europe</a> in the 16th century. It has been a Baptist church since 1950.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/st-olafs-church-tallinn.jpg" alt="St. Olaf's Church, Tallinn" width="320" height="480" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Olga Itenberg · CC BY 2.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:St_Olaf%27s_church,_Tallinn,_July_2008.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
